v1.3.15 (2026-06-23)
--------------------
Security hardening pass across auth, session, and registration-token handling.

Critical:
- C1: admin_password scrubbed from the token record once the p12 is
  downloaded / registration is completed — it no longer sits in
  registration_tokens.json after use
- C2: p12-raw endpoint now checks the revoked flag (was missing — a revoked
  invite's cert could still be pulled via that route)
- C3: /register/{token}/complete now checks `activated` before marking a
  token used/revoked, closing a state-skip path

High:
- H1: POST/PUT/DELETE /api/profiles now require a valid session (were
  unauthenticated — anyone who could reach the port could rewrite server
  connection profiles)
- H2: session cookie now set with secure=True (was False)
- H3: /api/login rate-limited to 10 attempts per IP per minute
- H4: /api/debug/* endpoints restricted to localhost only
- H5/H6: infoRows(), the cert card, and _renderCertView() now escape all
  server-supplied values before injecting into the DOM (XSS)

Low / medium:
- L4: cascade link table uses esc() and JSON.stringify for onclick
  attribute values instead of raw string interpolation
- M5: remote_host in .ovpn generation validated against a safe hostname
  regex before being written into the generated config
